{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Await"},{"type":"text","value":" component is a component that suspends until the provided promise is resolved or rejected.\nThis is only necessary for React 18.\nIf you are using React 19, you can use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"use()"},{"type":"text","value":" hook instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"await-props","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Await props"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Await"},{"type":"text","value":" component accepts the following props:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props-promise-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.promise"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise<T>"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The promise to await."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props-children-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.children"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(result: T) => React.ReactNode"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that will be called with the resolved value of the promise."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"await-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Await returns"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throws an error if the promise is rejected."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Suspends (throws a promise) if the promise is pending."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the resolved value of a deferred promise if the promise is resolved using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.children"},{"type":"text","value":" as the render function."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Await } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const { deferredPromise } = route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <Await promise={deferredPromise}>\n      {(data) => <div>{JSON.stringify(data)}</div>}\n    </Await>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"await-props","text":"Await props","level":2},{"id":"props-promise-prop","text":"props.promise prop","level":3},{"id":"props-children-prop","text":"props.children prop","level":3},{"id":"await-returns","text":"Await returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `Await` component is a component that suspends until the provided promise is resolved or rejected.\nThis is only necessary for React 18.\nIf you are using React 19, you can use the `use()` hook instead.\n\n## Await props\n\nThe `Await` component accepts the following props:\n\n### `props.promise` prop\n\n- Type: `Promise<T>`\n- Required\n- The promise to await.\n\n### `props.children` prop\n\n- Type: `(result: T) => React.ReactNode`\n- Required\n- A function that will be called with the resolved value of the promise.\n\n## Await returns\n\n- Throws an error if the promise is rejected.\n- Suspends (throws a promise) if the promise is pending.\n- Returns the resolved value of a deferred promise if the promise is resolved using `props.children` as the render function.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { Await } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const { deferredPromise } = route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <Await promise={deferredPromise}>\n      {(data) => <div>{JSON.stringify(data)}</div>}\n    </Await>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: awaitComponent\ntitle: Await component\n---\n\nThe `Await` component is a component that suspends until the provided promise is resolved or rejected.\nThis is only necessary for React 18.\nIf you are using React 19, you can use the `use()` hook instead.\n\n## Await props\n\nThe `Await` component accepts the following props:\n\n### `props.promise` prop\n\n- Type: `Promise<T>`\n- Required\n- The promise to await.\n\n### `props.children` prop\n\n- Type: `(result: T) => React.ReactNode`\n- Required\n- A function that will be called with the resolved value of the promise.\n\n## Await returns\n\n- Throws an error if the promise is rejected.\n- Suspends (throws a promise) if the promise is pending.\n- Returns the resolved value of a deferred promise if the promise is resolved using `props.children` as the render function.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { Await } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const { deferredPromise } = route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <Await promise={deferredPromise}>\n      {(data) => <div>{JSON.stringify(data)}</div>}\n    </Await>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
